evals/configure-routes.eval.ts / routes.text:
I've added a route resolver for blog posts in `prismic.config.json:1`:

```json
{
  "type": "blog_post",
  "path": "/blog/:category/:uid",
  "resolvers": { "category": "category" }
}
```

This maps `:category` to the UID of the document linked in blog_post's `category` content relationship field, and `:uid` to the post's own UID — producing URLs like `/blog/announcements/my-first-post`.

I converted the `page` custom type to a proper page type (`npx prismic type edit page --format page`), which gave it the `/:uid` route automatically, then added a scoped override route in `prismic.config.json` for the document with UID `home`, pointing it to `/`:

```json
{
  "repositoryName": "prismic-cli-isolated-0d20761a",
  "routes": [
    { "type": "page", "uid": "home", "path": "/" },
    { "type": "page", "path": "/:uid" }
  ]
}
```

So the page document with UID `home` resolves to `/`, and every other `page` document resolves to `/<uid>`. Want me to also push these model changes to the repo with `npx prismic push`?

